# Core Efficient Cursor Mode

Work with minimal context.

Rules:
- Do not scan the whole repository unless necessary.
- Do not load generated folders, logs, builds, media, node_modules, .next, dist, build, coverage, or cache folders.
- Identify only the 3 to 8 files relevant to the current task.
- Use focused search instead of full codebase scanning.
- Prefer small, safe edits.
- Do not activate MCP tools unless the task clearly requires them.
- Do not load unrelated rules.
- For Railway, Supabase, GitHub, Resend, Higgsfield, n8n, WhatsApp or Ollama tasks, use the matching rule/MCP only when explicitly needed.
- Keep plans short.
- Avoid long explanations unless requested.
- Do not touch secrets.
